  "learnings": [
    "WFS DefaultCRS is the publisher-declared default coordinate representation when srsName is omitted. Independently verify unchanged known IDs and all rings in that representation; do not claim the publisher internal datastore CRS or absolute survey accuracy. Prefer separately published storage/native CRS when available.",
    "GML 3.2 EPSG:4326 URN axes are north,east; GeoJSON uses east,north. Axis order follows the declared coordinate contract and is never fitted.",
    "A WMS group or raster coverage projection is not native parcel-vector CRS evidence. The DGI cadastre description enumerates 125 WCS raster coverages and no WFS feature type.",
    "A prior passed qualification is not a current read or native CRS proof. Source timeout, empty point response and unsupported direct-ID route must remain distinct from data absence."
  ],
  "coordinateReferences": [
    {
      "title": "OGC Web Feature Service 2.0.2 Interface Standard, DefaultCRS",
      "url": "https://docs.ogc.org/is/09-025r2/09-025r2.html",
      "claim": "DefaultCRS declares the coordinate representation used when no CRS is requested; it is not proof of internal storage CRS or survey accuracy."
    }
